Keeps public/ in git.

Next's standalone server serves this directory from the working directory, and
the Dockerfile copies it unconditionally. It held exactly one tracked file —
robots.txt — which was deleted when /robots.txt became a runtime route, and a
directory with no tracked files does not exist in a fresh checkout. The image
build then fails on `COPY --from=builder /app/public ./public`, which breaks the
whole release: both docs images are steps of the single build job that the
deploy job depends on.
